course: dictionary
lesson: 414
title: A careful judgement
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An appraisal is a careful judgement of how good, useful or valuable something or someone is. When you meet it in a text, look for someone weighing things up carefully.
explain: «An appraisal, or performance review, is a meeting where a boss talks through how someone has done over the year, a grown-up school report.» The words after the comma explain the hard word: a performance review is the same kind of thing, and a school report is something you already know.
explain: «Knowing the words (boss, colleague, appraisal, short-staffed) lets you understand what is really going on when work comes home.» The brackets give a list of work words, so appraisal must be about work. Try the swap: "a careful judgement of how someone has done at work" still makes sense.
explain: Appraisal can mean a meeting at work, an official value for money, or a careful judgement in general. Read the sentence to find which one is meant. Plain words for it are review, judgement and valuation.
fact: An appraisal is a careful judgement of how good, useful or valuable something or someone is.
fact: At work, an appraisal is a meeting where a manager talks with a worker about how well they are doing.
fact: With money, an appraisal is an official judgement of how much something, such as a house or a ring, is worth.
fact: «A performance appraisal» is a work review; «an appraisal of the damage» means a careful judgement of how bad the damage is.
fact: Plain words that mean nearly the same as appraisal are review, judgement and valuation.
exercise: «An appraisal, or performance review, is a meeting where a boss talks through how someone has done over the year.» What is an appraisal? | A list of jobs for the holidays | A party to celebrate the end of the year | A photo of a team at work | *A meeting where a boss talks through how someone has done over the year
exercise: «The family asked an expert for an appraisal of their house before they sold it.» What was the appraisal for? | To tell the neighbours about the sale | *To find out how much the house is worth | To paint the walls | To count the rooms for the dog
exercise: Which plain word means nearly the same as appraisal? | Garden | Breakfast | Holiday | *Judgement
test: Ravi's manager arranged a yearly appraisal with him to talk about his work. What kind of meeting is this? | A games club | *A work review | A shopping list | A school trip
test: «The appraisal of the ring said it was worth a lot of money.» Which meaning does appraisal have here? | A meeting at work | *An official judgement of how much something is worth | A quick nap | A party
exam: Mum waited for the official appraisal before she agreed a price for the house. What does appraisal mean here? | A meeting about the garden | *An official judgement of how much the house is worth | A holiday plan | A kind of cake
